      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Allowing item shaders on Quest avatars would not only expand the list of shaders that can be used; it would also make it less restricted in what we currently have for Quest shaders as a whole. The liquid shader for those potions I saw, and I think it was also used in the bubble gun item, could be interesting for avatars as well on Quest.\n\nThe reference cube on Quest has an Audiolink shader, while none of the whitelisted shaders have Audiolink support. I've already asked before for Audiolink support for Quest avatars for Toon Standard in a separate feature request before. But whitelisting those shaders for Quest would at least add some form of Audiolink for Quest as well.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-06-23T20:06:41.584Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Many vrchat items display features and shaders that VRChat quest avatars are forbidden to use. Things like a liquid shader on the bubble gun, a transparency shader that has a matcap on the sunglasses, these are things that quest avatars are not allowed to have. If the shaders are optimized enough to be used on the quest versions of official VRChat items, they should be whitelisted and made avalible in the Avatar SDK for Quest and iOS uploads.",
